# gadak TUI demo — list → filter → docs tree → doc detail → palette → quit
# Regenerated by `make media-tui`. Requires: vhs, tools/tapes/prepare.sh
#
# Sizing: the README renders this at 800 px, so the tape is deliberately small
# in *cells*, not in pixels. Fewer cells at a bigger font is the only lever on
# how large the text lands in the README — a wider terminal only makes the
# glyphs smaller. Measured grid for the values below: **77 cols × 24 rows**
# (VHS cell = 13.5 px at FontSize 20, plus 2×14 padding; verify with `stty size`
# in a throwaway tape after changing Width/FontSize). 77 is a balance point: at
# 72 the list's summary column collapses into ellipses, and past ~90 the glyphs
# land under 13 px in the README, which is the complaint this sizing answers.
#
# Size: VHS's own GIF encoder is generous. The committed asset is the tape
# output run through `gifsicle -O3 --colors 64` (see docs/MEDIA.md) — without
# that pass this lands around 7 MB against a 5 MB budget.
#
# Font: D2Coding is installed on this machine (fc-list / system_profiler).
# It covers Hangul so Korean status labels from the demo seed render aligned.
# If D2Coding is missing on another host, remove Set FontFamily (or point at
# Sarasa Mono K / Noto Sans Mono CJK) — without a CJK mono font, Hangul cells
# mis-width and columns drift.

Output docs/media/tui.gif

# Binary is built by tools/tapes/prepare.sh into tools/tapes/.tmp (on PATH via env.sh).

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 20
Set FontFamily "D2Coding, Menlo, Monaco, monospace"
Set Width 1080
Set Height 620
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set Padding 14
Set Framerate 8
Set TypingSpeed 70ms
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set BorderRadius 6

# Neutral shell: no user@host, no real $HOME path. `|| exit 1` is a safety
# interlock — without env.sh the take would run against the operator's default
# profile (~/.gadak) instead of the demo mirror.
Hide
Type "source tools/tapes/.tmp/env.sh || exit 1"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Show

Sleep 400ms

# Launch the navigator against the demo mirror.
Type "gadak tui"
Enter

# Wait until the list has rendered. +Screen matches the full buffer (not only
# the status bar line, which never contains issue keys). Match any project key
# — the default sort is by recency, so which project lands on top moves with
# the snapshot (waiting on /NMB-/ alone timed out once).
Wait+Screen@20s /NM[ABS]-/
Sleep 1.5s

# ── Filter: / then type ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Type "/"
Sleep 400ms
Type "pagination"
Sleep 1.5s
# Leave filter mode (filter text stays applied), then clear it so the docs
# beat starts from the full mirror.
Enter
Sleep 900ms
Type "/"
Sleep 200ms
Ctrl+U
Enter
Sleep 600ms

# ── Docs: D opens the mirrored wiki as a tree ──────────────────────────────
Type "D"
Wait+Screen@10s /PROD|ENG/
Sleep 1.6s

# Walk down a few pages so the tree indentation reads as a hierarchy.
Type "j"
Sleep 300ms
Type "j"
Sleep 300ms
Type "j"
Sleep 800ms

# Open one page: header breadcrumb (SPACE › ancestor › page) plus the body.
Enter
Sleep 2.5s
Escape
Sleep 700ms

# Back to the issue list.
Type "D"
Sleep 800ms

# ── Command palette ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ctrl+K
Sleep 1.4s
Escape
Sleep 500ms

Type "q"
Sleep 600ms
